The document’s skeleton — containers, regions, sections, the website page-set, and the section break.

<section #eh-article | `<article>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `document-containers` · eHTML `<article>` · JATS `<article>` · `content` `empty` → `<children>`

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `numbering-style` | kwarg | `arabic` `roman` `alpha` (default `arabic`) |  |
| `note-position` | kwarg | `bottom` `margin` (default `bottom`) | Document-level note render mode (#33): |

Produced by: canonical `<article>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code-block #code:eh-article-1>
<meta type=article>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
  <date | 2024-03-15>
</meta>

<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.

<section | Conclusion>
The paper concludes here.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-article-1>
<meta type=article>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
  <date | 2024-03-15>
</meta>

<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.

<section | Conclusion>
The paper concludes here.
</minipage>

*Typical authoring path: &lt;meta type=article&gt; at the top with no
&lt;article&gt; wrapper. The structural plugin generates the &lt;article&gt;
container and the three region wrappers. &lt;title&gt; in &lt;meta&gt; is
promoted to &lt;article-title&gt;; &lt;meta&gt; itself survives inside
&lt;article-front&gt;.*

<code-block #code:eh-article-2>
<article | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
<meta>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
</meta>

<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-article-2>
<article | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
<meta>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
</meta>

<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.
</minipage>

*Explicit-form escape hatch: &lt;article | Title&gt;. The structural plugin
respects the explicit wrapper. Pipe content from &lt;article&gt; becomes
&lt;article-title&gt;, placed as the first child of &lt;meta&gt; (creating
&lt;meta&gt; if absent, or appending if present).*

<code-block #code:eh-article-3>
<section | Introduction>
The introduction.

<section | Conclusion>
The conclusion.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-article-3>
<section | Introduction>
The introduction.

<section | Conclusion>
The conclusion.
</minipage>

*No &lt;meta&gt; and no &lt;article&gt; declared. The structural plugin assumes
article-shaped (the default) and wraps the sections in an implicit
article. &lt;article-front&gt; is omitted because there's no metadata.*

</section>

