<section #eh-book | `<book>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `document-containers` · eHTML `<book>` · JATS `<book>` · `content` `empty` → `<children>`

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `numbering-style` | kwarg | `arabic` `roman` `alpha` (default `arabic`) |  |
| `note-position` | kwarg | `bottom` `margin` (default `bottom`) | Document-level note render mode (#33): |

Produced by: canonical `<book>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code-block #code:eh-book-1>
<meta type=book>
  <title | A Natural History of Elephants>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
</meta>

<chapter | Origins>
<section | Early ancestors>
Content here.

<chapter | Modern populations>
<section | African elephants>
Content here.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-book-1>
<meta type=book>
  <title | A Natural History of Elephants>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
</meta>

<chapter | Origins>
<section | Early ancestors>
Content here.

<chapter | Modern populations>
<section | African elephants>
Content here.
</minipage>

*Typical authoring path: &lt;meta type=book&gt; at the top with no &lt;book&gt;
wrapper. The structural plugin generates &lt;book&gt; + the three region
wrappers. Each book-part contains its own &lt;meta&gt; with the promoted
&lt;book-part-title&gt;; no &lt;book-part-meta&gt; wrapper.*

<code-block #code:eh-book-2>
<meta type=book>
  <title | The Comprehensive Guide>
  <author | Author Name>
</meta>

<part | Part I: Foundations>
<chapter | First Principles>
Content.

<chapter | Background>
Content.

<part | Part II: Applications>
<chapter | Practical Examples>
Content.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-book-2>
<meta type=book>
  <title | The Comprehensive Guide>
  <author | Author Name>
</meta>

<part | Part I: Foundations>
<chapter | First Principles>
Content.

<chapter | Background>
Content.

<part | Part II: Applications>
<chapter | Practical Examples>
Content.
</minipage>

</section>

